From acf9acd3ce656344ff53bdecd4bfb4fda8969f33 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sami Slimani <slimsamister@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 22:07:31 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] port: concurrent draft cap through the draft backends

Strycast bounded each step's draft through a core change
(SpeculativeVerifier::VerifyStep max_draft_tokens and
StepRequest::max_draft_tokens). Gufo's verifier has no per-step bound, so the
runner sets the cap on the session's MTP or DFlash2 backend
(SetStepDraftCap), which clamps max_tokens where it enters a proposal: the
single, sampled, per-request and batched paths. The verifier accepts a shorter
proposal than it asked for, and the lookup copies and the DFlash2 length
controller read the bound from max_tokens as before, so the proposals match
the core cap's. A zero cap returns an empty proposal, which the verifier runs
as a target-only step.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
